From a99fddb8e4b61b0e1c1ea88c5cbbaa75b2728df6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:16:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: export set_direct_map_invalid_noflush for Apple DRM
 bring-up

Temporary Gravity early-alpha packaging workaround: appledrm is modular
and references this built-in ARM64 helper. Export it to GPL-compatible
modules without changing its implementation. Drop this patch when the
pinned downstream kernel carries the corresponding export or refactor.

Signed-off-by: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Assisted-By: OpenAI Codex (gpt-6-astra, gpt-5.6-sol)
---
 arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c b/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c
index 24d4f9357e974..f0dece2cf3afd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c
@@ -263,6 +263,7 @@ int set_direct_map_invalid_noflush(struct page *page)
 	return update_range_prot((unsigned long)page_address(page),
 				 PAGE_SIZE, set_mask, clear_mask);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(set_direct_map_invalid_noflush);
 
 int set_direct_map_default_noflush(struct page *page)
 {
